    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Recognize subtitles or lyrics from the draft or a segment.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id TEXT       Optional target segment id (raw id, no seg_id= prefix)\r\n          --language TEXT     Recognition language (BCP-47 code), e.g. zh / en / ja-JP\r\n          --recognize-type TEXT \r\n                              Subtitle recognize type: subtitle (default) / lyrics\r\n          --mode TEXT         Recognition scope: draft (whole draft) / segment (one target\r\n                              segment)\r\n          --timeout <duration> \r\n                              Execution timeout; explicit unit required, e.g. 5min or 300s\r\n          --poll-interval <duration> \r\n                              Progress poll interval; explicit unit required, e.g. 2s\r\n          --clear-previous TEXT \r\n                              Clear previously recognized results before writing: true / false\r\n                              (default true)\r\n          --translate-language-code TEXT \r\n                              Bilingual subtitle target language, e.g. en-US\r\n          --only-request-subtitles TEXT:{true,false} \r\n                              Return ASR sentences without writing subtitle tracks\r\n          --subtitle-source TEXT:{0,1,2,3} \r\n                              Subtitle source enum: 0 auto, 1 video, 2 sound, 3 audio\r\n          --clear-talking-head TEXT:{true,false} \r\n                              Clear talking-head subtitle state: true / false\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Recognize Chinese subtitles across the whole draft (mode=draft is implied)\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo subtitle-recognize --language zh\r\n  # Recognize lyrics instead of subtitles, keeping previous results\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo subtitle-recognize --recognize-type lyrics --clear-previous false\r\n  # Recognize a single segment\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo subtitle-recognize --language ja-JP --mode segment --seg-id <UUID>\r\n  # Recognize Japanese speech and write original plus Chinese subtitle tracks\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo subtitle-recognize --language ja-JP --translate-language-code zh-CN\r\n  # Return bilingual ASR sentences without modifying the draft\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo subtitle-recognize --language ja-JP --translate-language-code zh-CN --only-request-subtitles true\r\n  # Tune polling / timeout for long recognition jobs\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo subtitle-recognize --poll-interval 2s --timeout 5min\r\n\r\nNOTES\r\n  - `subtitle-recognize` supports omitting --seg-id in mode=draft.\r\n  - Use --seg-id when --mode segment.\r\n  - Omit --only-request-subtitles, or set it to false, to write subtitle tracks.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Recognize subtitles or lyrics from the draft or a segment.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id TEXT       Optional target segment id (raw id, no seg_id= prefix)\r\n          --language TEXT     Recognition language (BCP-47 code), e.g. zh / en / ja-JP\r\n          --recognize-type TEXT \r\n                              Subtitle recognize type: subtitle (default) / lyrics\r\n          --mode TEXT         Recognition scope: draft (whole draft) / segment (one target\r\n                              segment)\r\n          --timeout <duration> \r\n                              Execution timeout; explicit unit required, e.g. 5min or 300s\r\n          --poll-interval <duration> \r\n                              Progress poll interval; explicit unit required, e.g. 2s\r\n          --clear-previous TEXT \r\n                              Clear previously recognized results before writing: true / false\r\n                              (default true)\r\n          --translate-language-code TEXT \r\n                              Bilingual subtitle target language, e.g. en-US\r\n          --only-request-subtitles TEXT:{true,false} \r\n                              Return ASR sentences without writing subtitle tracks\r\n          --subtitle-source TEXT:{0,1,2,3} \r\n                              Subtitle source enum: 0 auto, 1 video, 2 sound, 3 audio\r\n          --clear-talking-head TEXT:{true,false} \r\n                              Clear talking-head subtitle state: true / false\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Recognize Chinese subtitles across the whole draft (mode=draft is implied)\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo subtitle-recognize --language zh\r\n  # Recognize lyrics instead of subtitles, keeping previous results\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo subtitle-recognize --recognize-type lyrics --clear-previous false\r\n  # Recognize a single segment\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo subtitle-recognize --language ja-JP --mode segment --seg-id <UUID>\r\n  # Recognize Japanese speech and write original plus Chinese subtitle tracks\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo subtitle-recognize --language ja-JP --translate-language-code zh-CN\r\n  # Return bilingual ASR sentences without modifying the draft\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo subtitle-recognize --language ja-JP --translate-language-code zh-CN --only-request-subtitles true\r\n  # Tune polling / timeout for long recognition jobs\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo subtitle-recognize --poll-interval 2s --timeout 5min\r\n\r\nNOTES\r\n  - `subtitle-recognize` supports omitting --seg-id in mode=draft.\r\n  - Use --seg-id when --mode segment.\r\n  - Omit --only-request-subtitles, or set it to false, to write subtitle tracks.\r\n",
